title the role is in the call graph
prompt Keaton said kg image/photos.rye -- sweep the densest single file left.
think Read the head and the pub boundary first. Fifteen exported verbs, crop through edges, ending at line 781, and everything past 1,100 named run_hue_turn, run_bilinear, run_saturate.
think Those are proofs, and no role-word vocabulary would ever have reached them. run_ is far too common a prefix to add -- caravan's run_supervisor is a real contract function.
think So the discriminator is not a name at all. A private function called only from a proof entry point is a proof whatever it is called, and that is a call-graph property.
obs Measured it before changing anything: 40 of the file's 244 asserts sit in the pub API, 200 in fourteen functions the selftest alone calls, 4 elsewhere.
think First draft of the reachability rule read 22,017 contract asserts as 10,285 -- the spread had swallowed the API, because a selftest calling the real API is exactly what a selftest is for. A pub function is never reached into, whatever calls it.
think Second guard: a private helper a pub function ALSO calls withdraws to contract, since shared code is contract code.
obs Spot-checked pond/apps/dexter_key.rye by eye before trusting the number. Its big holders are navigation_keys_decode and boundary_keys_are_harmless_no_ops -- test-case names called from run_selftest -- while pub drive and pub apply stay contracts. Correct.
obs image/photos.rye reads 49 contract, 49 covered, gap 0. It needed no sweep. Its 185 gap was proofs, and every real contract assert was already covered.
obs The arc, corrected four times: 13,235 -> 4,242 -> 3,978 -> 1,385, and coverage 59.6% -> 92%. Each correction was found by a hand opening a file and never by the meter.
obs Built the control rather than reporting the number, because a rule that moves a reading by an order of magnitude is a rule to prove. Fifteen behaviors on planted modules in a throwaway git pen, both failed drafts among them.
obs Swept nothing this round. The instruction named a file that needs nothing, and that is the second time -- both targets were named on numbers this meter produced.
